84748-85 | 2026-06-13T15:59:25Z | session:847487cd-e15b-4222-85ee-4a5a2b6f590b | **Changes:** \n - Removed `.take(8)` from the `feed.items` iteration. \n - Replaced the single `EmptyPanel("Loading highlights")` loading case with a distinct loading row containing a `CircularProgressIndicator` + "Syncing highlights…" text, tagged `Modifier.testTag("feed_loading")`. \n - The empty case (`feed.items.isEmpty()` after loading completes) retains `EmptyPanel("No highlights yet")` — clearly distinct from the loading state. \n - Items are now rendered in a `Column(modifier = Modifier.testTag("feed_item_list"))` wrapping `feed.items.forEach { }` with no cap. \n - Added imports: `CircularProgressIndicator`, `testTag` (deduplicated the `size` import that was accidentally doubled by the edit). [...] **One-sentence root cause:** The Android feed's render path, UniFFI type mapping, enum/field names, state plumbing, and core bridges are **byte-for-byte correct and symmetric with iOS** — so "zero cards" is **not** a Compose/mapping bug (the cards render the raw `quote`/`title` immediately with no hydration gate); an empty list can therefore only mean `state.homeFeed.items` is empty at the snapshot level (**option 1: data/auth/sync starvation in the core**), and the live emulator is in fact **logged out**, so a populated-feed repro was impossible without the prohibited sign-in. \n  \n **What I verified (and ruled out):** \n - **Option 3 (mapping)** — ruled out. Binding confirmed: `HighlighterHomeFeedItemKind = {HIGHLIGHTS, READ}`, fields `highlights: List<HydratedHighlight>`, `read: HighlighterHomeReadItem?`, etc. Android's `when(item.kind)` is exhaustive and reads exact field names. Identical to iOS. \n - **Option 4 (list not composed)** — ruled out. `OpenHomeFeed` dispatched once, `LazyColumn` renders `HomeFeedPanel(state.homeFeed)`, all items (the `take(8)` cap is already gone), no teardown loop. \n - **Option 2 (blank cards)** — ruled out as the *empty* cause. Both platforms render `quote`/`title` immediately. But there IS a real parity gap: **Android dispatches none** of `requestProfile`/`requestWebMetadata`/`requestIsbnPreview`/`article` that iOS fires from the cards — so Android cards look plain (raw quote, no resolved author/cover), not blank. \n - **Bridges** — both `listenForUpdates` AND `setCoreEventCallback` are wired on Android (`HighlighterViewModel.kt:69,227`), matching iOS. Not the missing-NMP-bridge issue. [...] - **Option 2 (blank cards)** — ruled out as the *empty* cause. Both platforms render `quote`/`title` immediately. But there IS a real parity gap: **Android dispatches none** of `requestProfile`/`requestWebMetadata`/`requestIsbnPreview`/`article` that iOS fires from the cards — so Android cards look plain (raw quote, no resolved author/cover), not blank. \n - **Bridges** — both `listenForUpdates` AND `setCoreEventCallback` are wired on Android (`HighlighterViewModel.kt:69,227`), matching iOS. Not the missing-NMP-bridge issue. [...]  \n | Card | Action | `LaunchedEffect` key | \n |---|---|---| \n | HIGHLIGHTS | `RequestProfile(lead.pubkey)` | `lead.pubkey` | \n | HIGHLIGHTS | `RequestIsbnPreview(isbn)` | `isbn` (bare ISBN string, e.g. `9780141187761`) | \n | HIGHLIGHTS (article) | `RequestProfile(articleAuthorPubkey)` | `articleAuthorPubkey` from `30023:<pubkey>:<dTag>` | \n | HIGHLIGHTS (web) | `RequestWebMetadata(url)` | `webUrl` (artifact preview URL or `sourceUrl`) | \n | READ | `RequestProfile(read.pubkey)` | `read.pubkey` | \n | READ | `RequestProfile(primaryInteractor)` | `primaryInteractor` (first of `interactorPubkeys`), keyed on `""` when absent | \n  \n Each `LaunchedEffect` fires exactly once per unique key value — no per-frame dispatch, matching iOS `.task(id:)` semantics. \n  \n --- \n  \n ### Existing components reused \n  \n - `AvatarImage` (from `ui/components/RemoteImage.kt`) — used for both the highlighter author byline and the article author byline and interactor avatar stack. This is the same component used in `CommentsPanel`, `AvatarButton`, etc. \n - `RemoteImage` (from `ui/components/RemoteImage.kt`) — used for cover images (56dp, `CoverShape`; 44dp for highlight resource header). \n - `LocalProfiles.current.profileFor(pubkey)` + `displayNameOr(pubkey)` + `avatarUrl()` (from `util/Profiles.kt`) — the same helpers `CommentsPanel` uses. \n - `LocalWebMetadata.current.webMetadataFor(url)` — existing helper from `util/Profiles.kt`. \n - `LocalIsbnPreviews.current.previewForIsbn(isbn)` — new helper added in this PR, same pattern. \n  [...]  \n The real cause of "Skipped 200-322 frames"/ANR is a **recomposition flood**: the core's `emit` (`nmp_app.rs:11093`) calls `onState` synchronously (uncoalesced — `emit_hz` is not applied at this layer) with a full `HighlighterAppState` clone on every resolved op. `onState` (`HighlighterViewModel.kt:201-204`) sets the `StateFlow`; `MainActivity.kt:75` collects it, so a burst of card-hydration ops → burst of full-snapshot emits → whole-tree recompositions on Main. The per-card `LaunchedEffect`s (`HomeFeedPanel.kt:187,202,218,238,409,416`) don't check whether the datum is already in state, amplifying the burst. \n  \n Core threading constraint: mutations are already serialized through the single actor thread; `dispatch` is safe from any thread (just `try_send`), so the host must NOT serialize calls itself. \n  \n **Fix (Android-side):** (1a) `sample`/conflate the collected `StateFlow` (`HighlighterViewModel.kt:58-59`) to coalesce bursts to ~1 recomposition/frame — high confidence this resolves the ANR; (1b) guard each hydration dispatch on absence from `LocalProfiles`/`LocalIsbnPreviews`/`LocalWebMetadata` in `HomeFeedPanel.kt`. Do NOT wrap `onState` in `Dispatchers.Main`. \n  [...]  \n **File:** `/Users/pablofernandez/Work/hl/app/android/app/src/main/java/com/highlighter/app/HighlighterViewModel.kt` \n  \n Added imports: `androidx.lifecycle.viewModelScope`, `SharingStarted`, `sample`, `stateIn`, `kotlin.time.Duration.Companion.milliseconds`. \n  \n Changed `state` from a direct `asStateFlow()` to a `by lazy` property that applies `.sample(16.milliseconds).stateIn(viewModelScope, SharingStarted.Eagerly, _state.value)`. The `@OptIn(FlowPreview::class)` annotation suppresses the API-preview warning. `onState` at line 201 is unchanged — it still writes `_state.value` directly from the core actor thread (thread-safe, no dispatch needed). `MainActivity.kt` calls `viewModel.state.collectAsState()` which works identically on the now-`StateFlow`-typed lazy property. \n  \n Coalescing approach: `sample(16 ms)` — drops all intermediate emissions during a burst and delivers only the latest value once per 16 ms window, bounding recomposition to ~1 per frame regardless of N simultaneous op resolutions. [...]  \n - Added `private var lastWifiOnly: Boolean? = null` field. \n - `init` block: sets `lastWifiOnly = initialWifiOnly` before the `syncNetworkCallback` call. \n - `onState`: now reads `wifiOnly = state.network.wifiOnlyEnabled`, compares to `lastWifiOnly`, and only calls `syncNetworkCallback` when the value has actually changed. On most state emissions during feed load, `wifiOnlyEnabled` is unchanged, so `syncNetworkCallback` (and its OS calls) is skipped entirely. \n  [...]  \n `HighlightsTab` hosted `HomeFeedPanel` as a **single `LazyColumn` item**: `item { HomeFeedPanel(...) }`. This gave no virtualization benefit — all 140+ cards were composed simultaneously as part of one giant lazy item. \n  \n There was no `verticalScroll` Column wrapping it (that concern from the task description turned out not to apply here), but the result was identical: every card was eagerly composed at once. \n  \n ### HomeFeedPanel.kt — converted to LazyListScope extension \n  \n `HomeFeedPanel` was rewritten from a `@Composable fun` that returned a `Column` into a `LazyListScope` extension function named `homeFeedItems`. The LazyListScope now emits: \n  \n - `item(key = "feed_header")` — the `SectionHeader` + Refresh button \n - `item(key = "feed_error")` — optional error text (only when non-blank) \n - `item(key = "feed_loading")` — loading spinner with `testTag("feed_loading")` (when isLoading && empty) \n - `item(key = "feed_empty")` — EmptyPanel (when !loading && empty) \n - `items(feed.items, key = { it.stableId })` — one lazy item per feed card, using `stableId` (a `String` field present on `HighlighterHomeFeedItem`) \n  \n The key field used is `item.stableId` — confirmed from the generated UniFFI binding at line 4960 of `highlighter_core.kt`. \n  [...] |---|---|---| \n | Janky frames | ~72% | **48.24%** | \n | Largest frame skip | 100–379 frames | **36 frames** | \n | Missed Vsync | (high) | 43 | \n | 50th / 90th pct | — | 36ms / 73ms | \n  \n **Verdict: jank materially improved** — janky frames dropped 24 percentage points, and the worst-case frame skip fell roughly 10x (from the 100–379 range to 36). Feed scrolling is smooth and tab navigation registers promptly. \n  \n The remaining ~48% is the expected next layer (heavy per-card content: remote images, hydration reads on visible cards) rather than the eager all-at-once realization that was the dominant cause — that root cause is now eliminated. If you want to push it further, the natural follow-ups would be image-load tuning and lightening the per-card composition, but the requested fix (eager `Column { forEach }` → single virtualized `LazyColumn`) is done and verified. \n 
