o-expire toast (`RootScene.kt`) \n  \n **File:** `/Users/pablofernandez/Work/hl/app/android/app/src/main/java/com/highlighter/app/ui/RootScene.kt` \n  \n Added `import kotlinx.coroutines.delay`. Inside the `state.toast?.let { toast -> ... }` block (lines 169-186), added a `LaunchedEffect(toast)` keyed on the toast object that `delay(4_000)`s then dispatches `HighlighterAppAction.ClearToast`. Each new distinct toast resets the timer. \n  [...] ## Issue 2 — "not found" toast: core-side emitter \n  \n `CoreError::NotFound`'s Display is literally `"not found"` (`core/src/errors.rs:20-21`). Three benign background per-card hydration paths surface it as a **global Error toast** via the raw error string: \n - `handle_web_metadata_resolved` — `nmp_app.rs:8969-8978` (web URL returns non-success/unparseable/cached-negative → `NotFound`, `web_metadata.rs:246,269,291`) \n - `handle_isbn_preview_resolved` — `nmp_app.rs:8898-8910` \n - `request_profile` subscribe failure — `nmp_app.rs:9536-9544` \n  \n These ops fire automatically per visible card, so any dead link/missing preview pops the banner on Highlights, Rooms, and Room detail. It's **persistent** because Android's `ToastBanner` (`Common.kt:118-142`) has no auto-expiry (only manual Dismiss), and new failures re-set it. iOS shows the same toast — its `ShareToastBanner` (`RootSceneView.swift:59-83`) also has no timer despite the misleading comment — confirming the emitter is shared/core-side. \n  \n **Fix (primary, core-side, fixes both platforms):** remove the `set_toast` calls in those three benign paths (log/insert a negative marker instead). **Secondary (Android safety net):** add a keyed `LaunchedEffect { delay; dispatch(ClearToast) }` in `RootScene.kt:169-186`. \n 
