ile(pubkeyHex)`. \n - **Source header tap (article)**: `HighlighterAppAction.OpenArticleReader(pubkeyHex, dTag, null)` — extracted from `"30023:<pubkey>:<dTag>"` address. Only shown when the address parses correctly. \n - **Bookmark**: `HighlighterAppAction.ToggleArticleBookmark(address)` — only for 30023 article-backed highlights (iOS parity: omitted/invisible for web/book/unknown). \n - **Share**: Android system share sheet (`Intent.ACTION_SEND`) with `https://beta.highlighter.com/highlight/<eventId>` — mirrors iOS `ShareLink(item: url)`. \n  \n --- \n  \n ## Feed card routing change \n  \n `HighlightFeedCard` is now `.clickable { onOpenDetail(leadHydrated) }` — tapping opens the **Highlight Detail screen**, not `OpenArticleReader`. The source reader (article/web) is reachable from *within* the detail via the tappable resource header. The `ReadingFeedCard` is unchanged (still dispatches `OpenArticleReader` directly — it's an article card, not a highlight card). \n  \n --- \n  \n ## Omitted (no binding) \n  \n - **ShareHighlightRepost** (`ShareHighlightRepost(eventId, authorPubkeyHex, relayHint, targetGroupId)`) requires a `targetGroupId` (room picker). Android has no room-picker sheet for highlights (iOS has `ShareToCommunitySheet`). Omitted — the system share fills the affordance instead. \n - **Web reader** from source header: no `OpenWebReader` or equivalent action in the binding; iOS dispatches to a `WebReaderTarget` navigation destination. Web URLs are recognized but the tap does nothing (omitted with a comment). \n - **Page image** (`HighlightPageImage.swift`'s `treatment: .feature`): rendered as a `RemoteImage` from `highlight.imageUrl` — the `imageUrl` field is confirmed in `HighlightRecord`. \n  \n --- \n  \n ## TestTags added \n  \n `highlight_detail`, `highlight_detail_author`, `highlight_detail_comment`, `highlight_detail_share`, `highlight_detail_bookmark` [...] Every screen that had a Refresh button already dispatches its Open action on appear: \n - HomeFeed: `DisposableEffect(Unit) { dispatch(OpenHomeFeed) }` in `HighlightsTab`. \n - RoomExplorer: `DisposableEffect(Unit) { dispatch(OpenRoomExplorer) }` in `RoomsTab`. \n - Bookmarks: `DisposableEffect(Unit) { dispatch(OpenBookmarks) }` in `MainScaffold`. \n - Feedback: `DisposableEffect(Unit) { dispatch(OpenFeedback(...)) }` in `MainScaffold`. \n - MediaSettings: `DisposableEffect(Unit) { dispatch(OpenMediaSettings) }` in `SettingsScreen`. \n - Comments, Profile, ArticleReader, RoomInvite: these are core-state-driven overlays (rendered when their state key is non-blank), meaning the calling screen already dispatched the Open action before the panel is even composed. No changes required. \n 
