84748-134 | 2026-06-13T17:29:16Z | session:847487cd-e15b-4222-85ee-4a5a2b6f590b |  \n `CoreError::NotFound`'s Display is literally `"not found"` (`core/src/errors.rs:20-21`). Three benign background per-card hydration paths surface it as a **global Error toast** via the raw error string: \n - `handle_web_metadata_resolved` — `nmp_app.rs:8969-8978` (web URL returns non-success/unparseable/cached-negative → `NotFound`, `web_metadata.rs:246,269,291`) \n - `handle_isbn_preview_resolved` — `nmp_app.rs:8898-8910` \n - `request_profile` subscribe failure — `nmp_app.rs:9536-9544` \n  \n These ops fire automatically per visible card, so any dead link/missing preview pops the banner on Highlights, Rooms, and Room detail. It's **persistent** because Android's `ToastBanner` (`Common.kt:118-142`) has no auto-expiry (only manual Dismiss), and new failures re-set it. iOS shows the same toast — its `ShareToastBanner` (`RootSceneView.swift:59-83`) also has no timer despite the misleading comment — confirming the emitter is shared/core-side. \n  \n **Fix (primary, core-side, fixes both platforms):** remove the `set_toast` calls in those three benign paths (log/insert a negative marker instead). **Secondary (Android safety net):** add a keyed `LaunchedEffect { delay; dispatch(ClearToast) }` in `RootScene.kt:169-186`. \n  [...] ### Fix 2 primary — Remove benign `set_toast` calls (`nmp_app.rs`) \n  \n **File:** `/Users/pablofernandez/Work/hl/app/core/src/nmp_app.rs` \n  \n Three `set_toast(Error, ...)` calls replaced with `tracing::debug!(...)`: \n  \n - `handle_isbn_preview_resolved` (~line 8903): `Err` arm → `tracing::debug!(isbn = %requested, error = %message, "isbn preview not found")` \n - `handle_web_metadata_resolved` (~line 8971): `Err` arm → `tracing::debug!(url = %requested, error = %message, "web metadata not found")` \n - `request_profile` subscribe failure (~line 9536): → `tracing::debug!(pubkey = %pubkey_hex, error = %err, "profile subscription failed")` (the `changed = true` is preserved) \n  \n This fixes both Android and iOS since the emitter is shared. \n  \n ### Fix 2 secondary — Auto-expire toast (`RootScene.kt`) \n  \n **File:** `/Users/pablofernandez/Work/hl/app/android/app/src/main/java/com/highlighter/app/ui/RootScene.kt` \n  \n Added `import kotlinx.coroutines.delay`. Inside the `state.toast?.let { toast -> ... }` block (lines 169-186), added a `LaunchedEffect(toast)` keyed on the toast object that `delay(4_000)`s then dispatches `HighlighterAppAction.ClearToast`. Each new distinct toast resets the timer. \n  [...] ### Fix 2 — "Welcome to Highlighter / Dismiss" banner overlapping the top header \n  \n **What the banner is:** The `ToastBanner` composable in `RootScene.kt`, driven by `state.toast` (a `HighlighterToast` the core emits, e.g. with message "Welcome to Highlighter"). With `enableEdgeToEdge()` active in `MainActivity`, the outer `Box(Modifier.fillMaxSize())` starts at the raw screen top edge. The old `padding(16.dp)` + `Alignment.TopCenter` placed the banner at 16dp from the physical top — below the status bar but squarely over the `TopAppBar` rendered inside the `MainScaffold`'s `Scaffold`. \n  \n **Fix in `/Users/pablofernandez/Work/hl/app/android/app/src/main/java/com/highlighter/app/ui/RootScene.kt`:** \n - Added `WindowInsets`, `asPaddingValues`, `statusBars` imports \n - Toast container padding changed to `top = WindowInsets.statusBars + 64.dp + 8.dp`, `start/end = 16.dp` — the `64.dp` is the standard M3 `TopAppBar` height, the `8.dp` is a comfortable visual gap; this matches how iOS's `ShareToastBanner` is positioned below the navigation bar via `.overlay(alignment: .top)` + `.padding(.top, 8)` [...]  \n Added `import kotlinx.coroutines.delay`. Inside the `state.toast?.let { toast -> ... }` block (lines 169-186), added a `LaunchedEffect(toast)` keyed on the toast object that `delay(4_000)`s then dispatches `HighlighterAppAction.ClearToast`. Each new distinct toast resets the timer. \n 
