84748-145 | 2026-06-13T17:49:17Z | session:847487cd-e15b-4222-85ee-4a5a2b6f590b | ## Summary \n  \n **Flows cataloged:** 38 concrete, validation-ready user flows (covering the three the user named — see-the-feed #6, open-a-room #12, OCR-capture #24 — plus the full breadth: auth, rooms, reading/books, profiles, comments, share, search, settings, podcast). \n  \n **Android state breakdown (mapped to the 38 flows):** ~26 WORKING, ~7 PARTIAL, 2 BROKEN, 3 MISSING. By area: ~22 areas WORKING, ~6 PARTIAL, 3 BROKEN, 4 MISSING items (one cohesive feature: OCR capture). \n  \n **Key finding (corrects the premise):** Android is **not** a dead shell. The Rust-core bridge (`HighlighterViewModel`: `listenForUpdates` + `setCoreEventCallback` armed pre-login + StateFlow dispatch), the auth gate (`RootScene`), the 3-tab scaffold, feed wiring, room explorer, room detail, profile, bookmarks, reader, search, and settings all render real core snapshots correctly. The "complete disaster" experience is produced by a **few high-impact defects** layered on a mostly-correct app. \n  \n **Top 5 critical fixes:** \n 1. `MainScaffold.kt:320` — `RoomsTab` onDispose wrongly dispatches `CloseRoom`, collapsing `roomDetail` and dismissing a just-opened room on any tab switch/recomposition. This is the real "opening rooms does nothing." *Tiny fix, highest impact.* \n 2. `MainScaffold.kt:331-333` — `CreateRoomPanel` is rendered as the permanent first item of the Rooms `LazyColumn` (the user's "Create Room form dumped at top"). iOS uses a `+` toolbar button → modal sheet. Relocate behind a FAB/toolbar affordance. \n 3. `HomeFeedPanel.kt:68` — silent `take(8)` cap + no loading-vs-empty distinction makes a syncing/paged feed look broken. The feed *is* wired (`OpenHomeFeed` fires); fix truncation + loading state. \n 4. OCR capture is genuinely MISSING — no CAMERA permission, no camera, no OCR, no ISBN entry/lookup (iOS has 15 capture files; Android has 1 gallery-pick stub). Largest phase; also never prime