()` exactly — then commits `HighlighterCaptureArtifact.Pending(committed)` as `selectedArtifact`. \n  \n **Publish path** \n - `selectedArtifact` is now `HighlighterCaptureArtifact?` (was `ArtifactRecord?`), passed directly to `PublishCaptureHighlight` and `PublishCapturePicture` — both already accept `HighlighterCaptureArtifact` / optional respectively, so no action-signature changes were needed. \n  \n --- \n  \n ### testTags added \n  \n | Tag | Element | \n |---|---| \n | `capture_book_recents` | `LazyRow` containing recent book cards | \n | `capture_recent_book` | Each `RecentBookCard` `Column` | \n | `capture_isbn_field` | Manual ISBN `OutlinedTextField` | \n | `capture_isbn_preview` | `IsbnPreviewCard` `Card` |
84748-150 | 2026-06-13T18:01:22Z | session:847487cd-e15b-4222-85ee-4a5a2b6f590b |  \n #### `CameraCapture.kt` — camera viewfinder + OCR pipeline \n - `CameraCaptureScreen`: full-screen CameraX `PreviewView` bound to `DEFAULT_BACK_CAMERA` with a shutter button. On capture, calls `captureAndOcr()`. \n - `captureAndOcr()`: suspending coroutine — takes photo via `ImageCapture.OnImageCapturedCallback`, applies rotation, JPEG-encodes at quality 90, runs `recognizeLines()` to get `List<OcrLine>`, calls `OcrStructureReconstructor.toMarkdown()` + `flattenForAlt()`, returns `CaptureResult(jpegBytes, width, height, ocrMarkdown, altText, lines)`. \n - `recognizeLines()`: wraps ML Kit `TextRecognition.getClient(TextRecognizerOptions.DEFAULT_OPTIONS)` as a coroutine; converts each `TextBlock.Line` bounding box to an `OcrLine` with pixel-coordinate top/bottom/left/right. \n - testTags: `capture_camera_button` (dismiss/back), `capture_take_photo` (shutter button). \n  \n #### `OcrStructureReconstructor.kt` — markdown reconstruction \n Direct Kotlin port of iOS `OCRStructureReconstructor.swift` + `OCRLine`/`OCRWord` structs: \n - `OcrLine` data class with `top/bottom/left/right/midY/height/width/midX`. \n - `OcrStructureReconstructor.toMarkdown(lines)`: normalize ligatures/zero-width chars → reading-order sort (two-column aware k-means on left edges) → `buildPageStats()` (median height, median gap, mode-binned body margins) → strip running headers/footers (page numbers and short edge lines) → `assembleMarkdown()` (body/heading1/heading2/listItem/blockQuote blocks, soft-join with hyphenation fusion, paragraph boundary heuristics). \n - `flattenForAlt(markdown)` — collapses `\n\n`/`\n` to spaces for the Blossom `alt` field. \n  \n #### `CapturePageReview.kt` — page review + quote selection \n - Shows captured page image (full bitmap from `jpegBytes`) in a card. \n - Upload status indicator while `isUploading`. \n - OCR markdown displayed in a `SelectionContainer` — Android's built-in text selection lets the user tap-and-drag to select text from the recognized output (testTag: `capture_ocr_text`). \n - `OutlinedTextField` below for the user to paste/type the exact quote (testTag: `capture_select_quote`). \n - "Use as quote" button → calls `findContext()` (finds the paragraph containing the quote) → calls `onQuoteSelected(quote, context)`. \n - "Retake" → `onDismiss`. \n  \n #### `IsbnBarcodeScanner.kt` — ISBN barcode scanner \n - Full-screen CameraX + `ImageAnalysis` pipeline (STRATEGY_KEEP_ONLY_LATEST, single-thread executor). \n - ML Kit `BarcodeScanning.getClient()` processes each frame; accepts `FORMAT_EAN_13`, `FORMAT_EAN_8`, `TYPE_ISBN`. \n - First raw barcode value is fed through `normalizeIsbn()` (the existing UniFFI binding); if non-null, fires `onResult(normalized13digit)` once and stops scanning.
