at dispatched `RefreshProfile`. \n - The `Row` remains because it still contains "Edit profile" (for own profile) and "Follow"/"Following" (for other profiles). \n - Removed now-unused `import BorderStroke` and `import OutlinedButton`. \n  \n **`ui/rooms/RoomInvitePanel.kt`** \n - Removed the `OutlinedButton` ("Loading"/"Refresh") that dispatched `RefreshRoomInvite` from lines 118-123. \n - Remaining buttons in the `Row` ("Link", "Add", "Close") are unchanged. \n  \n ## On-appear auto-load — no additions needed \n  \n Every screen that had a Refresh button already dispatches its Open action on appear: \n - HomeFeed: `DisposableEffect(Unit) { dispatch(OpenHomeFeed) }` in `HighlightsTab`. \n - RoomExplorer: `DisposableEffect(Unit) { dispatch(OpenRoomExplorer) }` in `RoomsTab`. \n - Bookmarks: `DisposableEffect(Unit) { dispatch(OpenBookmarks) }` in `MainScaffold`. \n - Feedback: `DisposableEffect(Unit) { dispatch(OpenFeedback(...)) }` in `MainScaffold`. \n - MediaSettings: `DisposableEffect(Unit) { dispatch(OpenMediaSettings) }` in `SettingsScreen`. \n - Comments, Profile, ArticleReader, RoomInvite: these are core-state-driven overlays (rendered when their state key is non-blank), meaning the calling screen already dispatched the Open action before the panel is even composed. No changes required. \n  \n ## Pull-to-refresh gestures intentionally left \n  \n `MainScaffold.kt` contains two `PullToRefreshBox` gesture wrappers: \n - Line 352-373: `HighlightsTab` — `onRefresh = { dispatch(RefreshHomeFeed) }` (pull gesture, not a button). \n - Line 389-417: `RoomsTab` — `onRefresh = { dispatch(RefreshRoomExplorer) }` (pull gesture, not a button). \n  \n Both are gesture-based (swipe-down) and were left in place per the task instructions. \n  \n ## Compile result \n  \n `./gradlew compileDebugKotlin` → **BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 6s** (1 task executed, 16 up-to-date, 0 errors, 0 warnings from the task itself). [...] ### 4. `app/android/app/src/main/java/com/highlighter/app/ui/home/HomeFeedPanel.kt` — guard debug log allocation \n  \n - Replaced the unconditional `android.util.Log.i(...)` call that built a `joinToString` string from the full `feed.items` list on every composition with a `Log.isLoggable(...)` guard. The `joinToString` allocation is now skipped in production (where the `highlighter-feed` tag is not at `INFO` level). \n  [...] ## Summary \n  \n **One-sentence root cause:** The Android feed's render path, UniFFI type mapping, enum/field names, state plumbing, and core bridges are **byte-for-byte correct and symmetric with iOS** — so "zero cards" is **not** a Compose/mapping bug (the cards render the raw `quote`/`title` immediately with no hydration gate); an empty list can therefore only mean `state.homeFeed.items` is empty at the snapshot level (**option 1: data/auth/sync starvation in the core**), and the live emulator is in fact **logged out**, so a populated-feed repro was impossible without the prohibited sign-in. \n  \n **What I verified (and ruled out):** \n - **Option 3 (mapping)** — ruled out. Binding confirmed: `HighlighterHomeFeedItemKind = {HIGHLIGHTS, READ}`, fields `highlights: List<HydratedHighlight>`, `read: HighlighterHomeReadItem?`, etc. Android's `when(item.kind)` is exhaustive and reads exact field names. Identical to iOS. \n - **Option 4 (list not composed)** — ruled out. `OpenHomeFeed` dispatched once, `LazyColumn` renders `HomeFeedPanel(state.homeFeed)`, all items (the `take(8)` cap is already gone), no teardown loop. \n - **Option 2 (blank cards)** — ruled out as the *empty* cause. Both platforms render `quote`/`title` immediately. But there IS a real parity gap: **Android dispatches none** of `requestProfile`/`requestWebMetadata`/`requestIsbnPreview`/`article` that iOS fires from the cards — so Android cards look plain (raw quote, no resolved author/cover), not blank. \n - **Bridges** — both `listenForUpdates` AND `setCoreEventCallback` are wired on Android (`HighlighterViewModel.kt:69,227`), matching iOS. 