e small opaque thumbnails; RGB_565 halves the bytes the decoder writes and uploads to the GPU vs ARGB_8888. This is the single biggest per-decode saving and directly satisfies task point 3. Coil keeps ARGB_8888 for images that need alpha. \n 2. **`allowHardware(true)`** — stated explicitly (it was already the default) so hardware bitmaps can never be silently disabled; decoded frames skip the CPU→GPU upload copy and stay off the Java heap. \n 3. **`bitmapFactoryMaxParallelism(8)`** — during a fast fling many cards request a decode at once; raising the ceiling stops decodes serialising behind a single worker and arriving late. \n 4. **Removed crossfade entirely** — the original baseline ran `crossfade(true)` on every request. A crossfade invalidates and redraws every frame of the fade for each newly-loaded image — pure main-thread work during the exact scroll where jank is measured. With many images fading in mid-fling this is a per-frame redraw storm. Dropping it removes that; images now appear when ready. Placeholders still work via the `surfaceVariant` background Box (unchanged). \n  \n API verification: `allowRgb565`, `allowHardware`, and `bitmapConfig` live in `coil3.request.ImageRequests_androidKt` (imports `coil3.request.allowRgb565`, `coil3.request.allowHardware`); `bitmapFactoryMaxParallelism` lives in `coil3.ImageLoaders_androidKt` (import `coil3.bitmapFactoryMaxParallelism`). All confirmed against the decompiled coil-core-android 3.2.0 aar — no invented APIs. \n  \n ### Unchanged from first iteration \n - Sized requests (`AvatarImage` always `.size(px)`; covers pass `targetSize` at 11 fixed-size call sites) — the core decode-resolution fix, retained. \n - Memory cache (25%) + disk cache (100 MB), shared via `SingletonImageLoader.Factory` auto-detection. \n - `RemoteImage`/`AvatarImage` public API unchanged (`targetSize` is optional, defaults to `null`). \n - Manifest registration of `HighlighterApplication`. \n  \n ### Behavior note \n The only user-visible behavior change is that images no longer fade in (they were fading before). This is intentional — the fade was a jank source. All placeholder/error/null-URL states are preserved. \n  \n **`compileDebugKotlin`:** `BUILD SUCCESSFUL`, no errors, no warnings. \n  \n The net effect on decode cost: each thumbnail is now decoded at slot resolution (sized requests), in RGB_565 (half the bytes), as a hardware bitmap (no upload copy), with no per-frame fade animation, and concurrent decodes no longer serialise. These are all directional reductions in the per-card decode work the validator is measuring.
