gnized output (testTag: `capture_ocr_text`). \n - `OutlinedTextField` below for the user to paste/type the exact quote (testTag: `capture_select_quote`). \n - "Use as quote" button → calls `findContext()` (finds the paragraph containing the quote) → calls `onQuoteSelected(quote, context)`. \n - "Retake" → `onDismiss`. \n  \n #### `IsbnBarcodeScanner.kt` — ISBN barcode scanner \n - Full-screen CameraX + `ImageAnalysis` pipeline (STRATEGY_KEEP_ONLY_LATEST, single-thread executor). \n - ML Kit `BarcodeScanning.getClient()` processes each frame; accepts `FORMAT_EAN_13`, `FORMAT_EAN_8`, `TYPE_ISBN`. \n - First raw barcode value is fed through `normalizeIsbn()` (the existing UniFFI binding); if non-null, fires `onResult(normalized13digit)` once and stops scanning. \n - Corner-bracket reticle overlay drawn with a `Surface` border; dismiss button top-left (testTag: `capture_scan_barcode`). \n  \n #### `CapturePanel.kt` — fully rewritten, orchestrates the three phases \n Three-phase internal enum: `Idle → Camera → Review`. From `Idle`: \n - "Camera" button checks/requests the runtime CAMERA permission, then enters `Camera` phase. \n - "Photo" button retains the existing gallery-picker path. \n - ISBN row now has a "Scan" `OutlinedButton` (testTag `capture_scan_barcode`) next to "Find"; tapping it shows `IsbnBarcodeScannerScreen` as an in-panel overlay; detected ISBN feeds straight into the existing `RequestIsbnPreview` / preview-card flow. \n  \n In `Camera` phase: `CameraCaptureScreen` is shown full-screen. On capture, `UploadCapturePhoto(bytes, "image/jpeg", width, height, altText)` is dispatched immediately (upload runs in parallel with review), then transitions to `Review` phase. \n  \n In `Review` phase (`CapturePanelReviewWrapper`): \n - Step 1 (`CapturePageReview`): image + OCR text, quote selection → saves `quote` + `context`. \n - Step 2 (publish metadata): quote editor, note, compact recent-books row, community picker. \n - Publish button dispatches `PublishCapture