s the same toast — its `ShareToastBanner` (`RootSceneView.swift:59-83`) also has no timer despite the misleading comment — confirming the emitter is shared/core-side. \n  \n **Fix (primary, core-side, fixes both platforms):** remove the `set_toast` calls in those three benign paths (log/insert a negative marker instead). **Secondary (Android safety net):** add a keyed `LaunchedEffect { delay; dispatch(ClearToast) }` in `RootScene.kt:169-186`. \n  [...] ### Fix 2 primary — Remove benign `set_toast` calls (`nmp_app.rs`) \n  \n **File:** `/Users/pablofernandez/Work/hl/app/core/src/nmp_app.rs` \n  \n Three `set_toast(Error, ...)` calls replaced with `tracing::debug!(...)`: \n  \n - `handle_isbn_preview_resolved` (~line 8903): `Err` arm → `tracing::debug!(isbn = %requested, error = %message, "isbn preview not found")` \n - `handle_web_metadata_resolved` (~line 8971): `Err` arm → `tracing::debug!(url = %requested, error = %message, "web metadata not found")` \n - `request_profile` subscribe failure (~line 9536): → `tracing::debug!(pubkey = %pubkey_hex, error = %err, "profile subscription failed")` (the `changed = true` is preserved) \n  \n This fixes both Android and iOS since the emitter is shared. \n  \n ### Fix 2 secondary — Auto-expire toast (`RootScene.kt`) \n  \n **File:** `/Users/pablofernandez/Work/hl/app/android/app/src/main/java/com/highlighter/app/ui/RootScene.kt` \n  \n Added `import kotlinx.coroutines.delay`. Inside the `state.toast?.let { toast -> ... }` block (lines 169-186), added a `LaunchedEffect(toast)` keyed on the toast object that `delay(4_000)`s then dispatches `HighlighterAppAction.ClearToast`. Each new distinct toast resets the timer. \n 
