84748-212 | 2026-06-14T09:17:13Z | session:847487cd-e15b-4222-85ee-4a5a2b6f590b | ### Fix 2 — "Welcome to Highlighter / Dismiss" banner overlapping the top header \n  \n **What the banner is:** The `ToastBanner` composable in `RootScene.kt`, driven by `state.toast` (a `HighlighterToast` the core emits, e.g. with message "Welcome to Highlighter"). With `enableEdgeToEdge()` active in `MainActivity`, the outer `Box(Modifier.fillMaxSize())` starts at the raw screen top edge. The old `padding(16.dp)` + `Alignment.TopCenter` placed the banner at 16dp from the physical top — below the status bar but squarely over the `TopAppBar` rendered inside the `MainScaffold`'s `Scaffold`. \n  \n **Fix in `/Users/pablofernandez/Work/hl/app/android/app/src/main/java/com/highlighter/app/ui/RootScene.kt`:** \n - Added `WindowInsets`, `asPaddingValues`, `statusBars` imports \n - Toast container padding changed to `top = WindowInsets.statusBars + 64.dp + 8.dp`, `start/end = 16.dp` — the `64.dp` is the standard M3 `TopAppBar` height, the `8.dp` is a comfortable visual gap; this matches how iOS's `ShareToastBanner` is positioned below the navigation bar via `.overlay(alignment: .top)` + `.padding(.top, 8)` \n  [...] User: [Agent task result: Agent "Diagnose not-found toast + UI jank" completed] \n Both issues diagnosed; spec written to `/Users/pablofernandez/Work/hl/Plans/responsiveness-and-toast-fix.md`. \n  \n ## Issue 1 — Jank/ANR: the bridge does NOT block the UI thread \n  \n The Android→core path is non-blocking. `viewModel::dispatch` (`HighlighterViewModel.kt:114-116`) → `HighlighterNmpApp::dispatch` (`core/src/nmp_app.rs:1812-1816`) only does `tx.try_send(...)` into a bounded channel. The action body — including every `block_on_local` (`refresh_home_feed`/`refresh_room_detail`) — runs on a dedicated background thread `highlighter-nmp-actor` (`nmp_app.rs:2513`). So the `block_on_local exceeded budget` warnings are on the actor thread, not the UI thread. \n  \n The real cause of "Skipped 200-322 frames"/ANR is a **recomposition flood**: the core's `emit` (`nmp_app.rs:11093`) calls `onState` synchronously (uncoalesced — `emit_hz` is not applied at this layer) with a full `HighlighterAppState` clone on every resolved op. `onState` (`HighlighterViewModel.kt:201-204`) sets the `StateFlow`; `MainActivity.kt:75` collects it, so a burst of card-hydration ops → burst of full-snapshot emits → whole-tree recompositions on Main. The per-card `LaunchedEffect`s (`HomeFeedPanel.kt:187,202,218,238,409,416`) don't check whether the datum is already in state, amplifying the burst. \n  \n Core threading constraint: mutations are already serialized through the single actor thread; `dispatch` is safe from any thread (just `try_send`), so the host must NOT serialize calls itself. \n  \n **Fix (Android-side):** (1a) `sample`/conflate the collected `StateFlow` (`HighlighterViewModel.kt:58-59`) to coalesce bursts to ~1 recomposition/frame — high confidence this resolves the ANR; (1b) guard each hydration dispatch on absence from `LocalProfiles`/`LocalIsbnPreviews`/`LocalWebMetadata` in `HomeFeedPanel.kt`. Do NOT wrap `onState` in `Dispatchers.Main`. \n  \n ## Issue 2 — "not found" toast: core-side emitter \n  \n `CoreError::NotFound`'s Display is literally `"not found"` (`core/src/errors.rs:20-21`). Three benign background per-card hydration paths surface it as a **global Error toast** via the raw error string: \n - `handle_web_metadata_resolved` — `nmp_app.rs:8969-8978` (web URL returns non-success/unparseable/cached-negative → `NotFound`, `web_metadata.rs:246,269,291`) \n - `handle_isbn_preview_resolved` — `nmp_app.rs:8898-8910` \n - `request_profile` subscribe failure — `nmp_app.rs:9536-9544` \n  \n These ops fire automatically per visible card, so any dead link/missing preview pops the banner on Highlights, Rooms, and Room detail. It's **persistent** because Android's `ToastBanner` (`Common.kt:118-142`) has no auto-expiry (only manual Dismiss), and new failures re-set it. iOS shows the same toast — its `ShareToastBanner` (`RootSceneView.swift:59-83`) also has no timer despite the misleading comment — confirming the emitter is shared/core-side. \n  \n **Fix (primary, core-side, fixes both platforms):** remove the `set_toast` calls in those three benign paths (log/insert a negative marker instead). **Secondary (Android safety net):** add a keyed `LaunchedEffect { delay; dispatch(ClearToast) }` in `RootScene.kt:169-186`. \n  \n **Confidence:** High on both root causes and the exact emitter/thread lines. The only file the other agent owns — `ui/rooms/RoomDetailPanel.kt` — is explicitly excluded from all proposed edits. \n  \n Assistant: Sharp diagnosis — and good news on the scary one: the jank is **not** a UI-thread block (the core actor runs on its own thread). It's a **recomposition flood** — the core emits a full-state snapshot on every resolved op, uncoalesced, and the per-card hydration effects don't dedupe. Fixes are clear and Android-side. The "not found" toast is a core-side emitter firing on three benign per-card lookup failures (dead links / missing previews). \n  [...] User: [Agent task result: Agent "Fix UI jank + not-found toast" completed] \n All four fixes are implemented and both verification gates pass cleanly. \n  \n --- \n  \n ## Summary \n  \n ### Fix 1a — StateFlow coalescing (`HighlighterViewModel.kt`) \n  \n **File:** `/Users/pablofernandez/Work/hl/app/android/app/src/main/java/com/highlighter/app/HighlighterViewModel.kt` \n  \n Added imports: `androidx.lifecycle.viewModelScope`, `SharingStarted`, `sample`, `stateIn`, `kotlin.time.Duration.Companion.milliseconds`. \n  \n Changed `state` from a direct `asStateFlow()` to a `by lazy` property that applies `.sample(16.milliseconds).stateIn(viewModelScope, SharingStarted.Eagerly, _state.value)`. The `@OptIn(FlowPreview::class)` annotation suppresses the API-preview warning. `onState` at line 201 is unchanged — it still writes `_state.value` directly from the core